course: dictionary
lesson: 11985
title: Medical words: cervical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cervical is a long word for a body part, but you can work out a lot from the words around it. «The doctor checked her cervical spine after the fall.» The word spine is a clue: your spine is your back bone, and the cervical part is the top, near the head. So cervical must be about the neck.
explain: Cervical has two meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. «He wore a soft cervical collar to keep his neck still.» A collar goes around the neck, so here cervical means to do with the neck. Doctors also use the word for the cervix, a part inside a woman's body. You will meet that meaning in health lessons when you are older.
explain: When you meet a hard medical word, ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. Does «the doctor checked her neck bones after the fall» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Cervical means to do with the neck, or to do with the cervix.
fact: «Cervical vertebrae» are the seven bones in your neck.
fact: Almost all mammals have seven cervical vertebrae, even giraffes, whose necks are very long.
fact: «Cervical» comes from the Latin word «cervix», which means neck.
fact: A «cervical collar» is a soft support worn around the neck after an injury.
fact: «Cervical screening» is a health check that women are invited to have, to help find problems early.
exercise: «The doctor checked her cervical spine after the fall.» Which part of the body is the cervical spine? | The fingers | The knee | *The neck | The stomach
exercise: Most mammals, even giraffes, have how many cervical vertebrae? | Two | *Seven | Twelve | Twenty-four
exercise: «He wore a soft cervical collar to keep his neck still.» What does cervical mean in this sentence? | *To do with the neck | To do with the head | To do with the feet | Very soft
test: «Mum went for a cervical screening, a check to help find problems early.» What is a cervical screening? | A football match | A haircut at the hairdresser | *A health check of the cervix, a part of a woman's body | A test of how well you can see
test: Which bones are the cervical vertebrae? | The bones in your ribs | The bones in your fingers | The bones in your ears | *The bones in your neck
exam: What does cervical mean? | Very cold and icy | *To do with the neck or the cervix | To do with the ears and hearing | Happy and loud
